{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Potential.LogPotential\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp\n\n/-!\n# Log Potential Thermodynamics\n\nA structural layer over `LogPotential` for Jaynes / convex-thermo workflows:\n\n- `ψ` (Massieu / log-partition potential)\n- Fenchel gap\n- Legendre-contact packaging\n- entropy/free-energy style derived quantities\n- primal/dual Bregman divergences\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry\nnamespace LogPotential\n\n/-- A Legendre-style package over a scalar log-potential `ψ`. -/\nstructure LegendreModel where\n  L : LogPotential ℝ\n  /-- Candidate dual coordinate map `η = ∇ψ(θ)` (kept abstract at this layer). -/\n  grad : ℝ → ℝ\n  /-- Candidate dual potential `φ(η)`. -/\n  φ : ℝ → ℝ\n  /-- Fenchel inequality `θη ≤ ψ(θ) + φ(η)`. -/\n  fenchel_ineq : ∀ θ η, θ * η ≤ L.ψ θ + φ η\n  /-- Contact equality at the chosen dual coordinate `η = grad θ`. -/\n  contact : ∀ θ, φ (grad θ) = θ * grad θ - L.ψ θ\n\nnamespace LegendreModel\n\n/-- Massieu potential (log-partition in statistical mechanics conventions). -/\ndef massieu (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  M.L.ψ θ\n\n/-- Partition function recovered from the log-potential: `Z = exp ψ`. -/\nnoncomputable def partition (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  Real.exp (M.massieu θ)\n\n/-- Dual coordinate (typically the expectation parameter). -/\ndef dualCoord (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  M.grad θ\n\n/-- Fenchel gap `ψ(θ) + φ(η) - θη`, nonnegative by Fenchel inequality. -/\ndef fenchelGap (M : LegendreModel) (θ η : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  M.massieu θ + M.φ η - θ * η\n\n/-- Generic \"entropy-like\" quantity from the contact identity: `S = θη - ψ`. -/\ndef entropy (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  θ * M.dualCoord θ - M.massieu θ\n\n/-- A scaled free-energy convention: `F_ε = - ε ψ`. -/\ndef freeEnergy (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  -ε * M.massieu θ\n\n/-- Primal Bregman divergence generated by `ψ`. -/\nnoncomputable def primalBregman (M : LegendreModel) (θ θ₀ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  M.L.bregman θ θ₀\n\n/-- Dual Bregman divergence generated by `φ`. -/\nnoncomputable def dualBregman (M : LegendreModel) (η η₀ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  bregmanDiv M.φ η η₀\n\n@[simp] lemma massieu_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.massieu θ = M.L.ψ θ := rfl\n\n@[simp] lemma partition_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.partition θ = Real.exp (M.L.ψ θ) := rfl\n\n@[simp] lemma dualCoord_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.dualCoord θ = M.grad θ := rfl\n\n@[simp] lemma fenchelGap_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ η : ℝ) :\n    M.fenchelGap θ η = M.L.ψ θ + M.φ η - θ * η := rfl\n\nlemma fenchelGap_nonneg (M : LegendreModel) (θ η : ℝ) :\n    0 ≤ M.fenchelGap θ η := by\n  unfold fenchelGap massieu\n  linarith [M.fenchel_ineq θ η]\n\n/-- Contact identity rewritten as `entropy = φ(η)` at `η = grad θ`. -/\nlemma entropy_eq_dual_at_contact (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.entropy θ = M.φ (M.dualCoord θ) := by\n  unfold entropy dualCoord massieu\n  simpa using (M.contact θ).symm\n\n/-- Fenchel gap vanishes on the Legendre contact locus. -/\nlemma fenchelGap_eq_zero_at_contact (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.fenchelGap θ (M.dualCoord θ) = 0 := by\n  unfold fenchelGap dualCoord massieu\n  rw [M.contact θ]\n  ring\n\n/-- Equivalent form of the contact identity: `ψ + φ = θη` at `η = grad θ`. -/\nlemma contact_balance (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.massieu θ + M.φ (M.dualCoord θ) = θ * M.dualCoord θ := by\n  unfold massieu dualCoord\n  have h := M.contact θ\n  linarith\n\n/-- Free energy is just a scaled negative Massieu potential by definition. -/\n@[simp] lemma freeEnergy_def (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) :\n    M.freeEnergy ε θ = -ε * M.L.ψ θ := rfl\n\n/-- Canonical-ensemble energy convention:\nfor Gibbs weights `exp(-θ f)`, one usually has `U = -∂ψ/∂θ`,\nso from the abstract dual coordinate `η = grad θ` we define `U := -η`. -/\ndef canonicalEnergy (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  -M.dualCoord θ\n\n/-- Canonical entropy in Gibbs sign convention:\n`S = ψ + θ U = ψ - θη`. -/\ndef canonicalEntropy (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  M.massieu θ + θ * M.canonicalEnergy θ\n\n/-- Canonical free-energy notation (same scalar definition as `freeEnergy`). -/\ndef canonicalFreeEnergy (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  -ε * M.massieu θ\n\n/-- `ε`-scaled Fenchel gap, useful as a thermodynamic defect at scale `ε`. -/\ndef scaledFenchelGap (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ η : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  ε * M.fenchelGap θ η\n\n@[simp] lemma canonicalEnergy_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalEnergy θ = -M.dualCoord θ := rfl\n\n@[simp] lemma canonicalEntropy_def (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalEntropy θ = M.massieu θ - θ * M.dualCoord θ := by\n  unfold canonicalEntropy canonicalEnergy\n  ring\n\n@[simp] lemma canonicalFreeEnergy_def (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalFreeEnergy ε θ = -ε * M.massieu θ := rfl\n\n@[simp] lemma scaledFenchelGap_def (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ η : ℝ) :\n    M.scaledFenchelGap ε θ η = ε * (M.massieu θ + M.φ η - θ * η) := by\n  simp [scaledFenchelGap, fenchelGap]\n\n/-- The abstract convex-conjugate entropy and canonical entropy are opposites\nunder the Gibbs-sign convention. -/\nlemma canonicalEntropy_eq_neg_entropy (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalEntropy θ = -M.entropy θ := by\n  unfold canonicalEntropy canonicalEnergy entropy dualCoord massieu\n  ring\n\n/-- Contact identity in canonical sign convention:\n`S = -φ(η)` at `η = grad θ`. -/\nlemma canonicalEntropy_eq_neg_dual_at_contact (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalEntropy θ = -M.φ (M.dualCoord θ) := by\n  calc\n    M.canonicalEntropy θ = -M.entropy θ := M.canonicalEntropy_eq_neg_entropy θ\n    _ = -M.φ (M.dualCoord θ) := by\n      rw [M.entropy_eq_dual_at_contact]\n\n/-- Fenchel gap is nonnegative; scaled gap is nonnegative for nonnegative scale `ε`. -/\nlemma scaledFenchelGap_nonneg\n    (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ η : ℝ) (hε : 0 ≤ ε) :\n    0 ≤ M.scaledFenchelGap ε θ η := by\n  unfold scaledFenchelGap\n  exact mul_nonneg hε (M.fenchelGap_nonneg θ η)\n\n/-- Scaled Fenchel gap vanishes on the contact locus. -/\nlemma scaledFenchelGap_eq_zero_at_contact\n    (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) :\n    M.scaledFenchelGap ε θ (M.dualCoord θ) = 0 := by\n  unfold scaledFenchelGap\n  rw [M.fenchelGap_eq_zero_at_contact]\n  ring\n\n/-- Contact balance rewritten with canonical energy:\n`ψ = S - θ U` (Massieu form). -/\nlemma massieu_eq_canonicalEntropy_minus_theta_energy\n    (M : LegendreModel) (θ : ℝ) :\n    M.massieu θ = M.canonicalEntropy θ - θ * M.canonicalEnergy θ := by\n  unfold canonicalEntropy\n  ring\n\n/-- Canonical free energy is `-ε ψ`, so equivalently `-ε (S - θU)` in this sign convention. -/\nlemma canonicalFreeEnergy_eq_scaled_entropy_energy\n    (M : LegendreModel) (ε θ : ℝ) :\n    M.canonicalFreeEnergy ε θ\n      = -ε * (M.canonicalEntropy θ - θ * M.canonicalEnergy θ) := by\n  unfold canonicalFreeEnergy\n  rw [M.massieu_eq_canonicalEntropy_minus_theta_energy]\n\nend LegendreModel\n\nend LogPotential\nend InfoGeometry\n","mtime":1776602622061}